<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Commune of Mantua</h1><p class="st-meta">1115 CE – 1272 CE (approx.) · capital Mantua</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A lake-ringed city-republic of the Po plain that emerged after Matilda of Canossa's death and ended when the Bonacolsi seized power in 1272.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-mantua">Mantua</a> had been a centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matilda-of-tuscany">Matilda of Canossa's</a> lands. After her death in 1115 its citizens organised a commune under consuls, taking control of the city and the countryside from the old feudal lords and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The commune was governed by consuls and later a podestà. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-mantua">Mantua</a> joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lombard-league">Lombard League</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> and in the late 12th century engineer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alberto-pitentino">Alberto Pitentino</a> regulated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mincio">Mincio</a> to form the lakes that still surround the city. Mantua traded along the Po and the Mincio and fought neighbours such as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-verona">Verona</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-cremona">Cremona</a>. The troubadour poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sordello">Sordello</a> came from its territory.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1272 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pinamonte-bonacolsi">Pinamonte Bonacolsi</a> made himself captain of the people and ruled as lord, ending communal government. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-gonzaga">Gonzaga</a> overthrew the Bonacolsi in 1328, founding what became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-mantua">Duchy of Mantua</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/commune-of-mantua.jpg" alt="Commune of Mantua" width="320" height="214"><figcaption>Image: EdoM · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dsc_1150_Mantua.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1115 CE – 1272 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mantua</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Lombard, Emilian, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Mantua (commune)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1194&amp;focus=commune-of-mantua" aria-label="Commune of Mantua on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4937 584 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Commune of Mantua lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5257 840L5257 840"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5257 840h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5257 840h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5257 840h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1194&amp;focus=commune-of-mantua">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
